research/wave7-dispatch/orchestrator-A3-judgment.log-18552-The source states the divergent-series Abel–Dini–Pringsheim theorem for positive terms with inclusive partial sums S_n: sum a_n/S_n diverges and sum a_n/S_n^t converges for t>1, hence in particular at t=2. These are exactly the item's two claims and convention. The local proof derives the two estimates directly from Cauchy and telescoping facts.
