research/wave7-dispatch/orchestrator-A3-judgment.log-19082-Let $p \in \mathbb{Q}$ with $p > 0$. Condensation ([[thm-cauchy-condensation]]) applied to the family $a_k = 1/k^{p}$, $k \ge 1$, produces a **geometric series of ratio $2^{\,1-p}$**: $$2^{j} a_{2^{j}} \;=\; 2^{j}\big(2^{j}\big)^{-p} \;=\; 2^{\,(1-p)j} \;=\; \big(2^{\,1-p}\big)^{j} \qquad (j \in \mathbb{N}).$$ So the whole $p$-series family collapses onto the single question of when a geometric ratio is below $1$, and the threshold $p = 1$ is where $2^{\,1-p} = 2^{0} = 1$. That is the computation behind [[thm-p-series-rational]], displayed here on its own and instantiated at three exponents: | $p$ | ratio $2^{\,1-p}$ | condensed series | verd
