research/audit/wave7-refuter-tasks/cex-limit-comparison-l-zero-one-directional.md-74-[L3] $\sum_{k \ge 1} 1/k^{p}$ converges if and only if $p > 1$; at $p = 2$ it converges ([[thm-p-series-rational]], [[def-rational-power]]).
