research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-606207-
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-606208-**Given:** The sequence $a_k := 1/\iota(k+1)$, $k \in \mathbb{N}$, and its inclusive partial sums $S_n = \sum_{k=0}^{n} a_k$ ([[def-series]], [[def-finite-sum]], [[lem-of-naturals-positive]]).
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-606209-
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-606210-[L1] The canonical naturals are positive, so each $a_k$ is positive and each $S_n$ is a sum of positive terms ([[lem-of-naturals-positive]], [[lem-of-inverse-positive]]).
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-606211-
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log:606212:[L2] The harmonic series $\sum_{k \ge 1} 1/k$ diverges ([[ex-harmonic-series-diverges]]), and it is by definition the series of $j \mapsto 1/\iota(j+1)$ ([[def-series]]).
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-606213-
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-606214-[L3] Abel-Dini: for a sequence of positive terms whose series diverges, with $S_n$ the inclusive partial sums, $\sum_n a_n/S_n$ diverges and $\sum_n a_n/S_n^{2}$ converges ([[thm-abel-dini]], [[def-integer-power]]).
