The core proof checks out: dyadic blocks give the stated \(1/2\) bound, induction gives \(A_{2^n}\ge1+n/2\), Archimedean cofinality makes those partial sums unbounded, and condensation then gives divergence. The source-backed Oresme block argument is also present in Hunter’s cited text.
